    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20a38ccf_04dba05a",
        "filename": "common/keyboard_8042.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1523797
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-27T22:04:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d prefer not using a variable in memory since it\u0027d just be a copy of a constant. I could change it to use `CONFIG_CMD_KEYBOARD_KBLOG_LEN` directly, but I think that\u0027s longer length-wise. `ARRAY_SIZE(kblog.ringbuf)` has the advantage of getting the exact element count of the buffer even if somebody changes the struct declaration later.",
      "parentUuid": "d8f03935_c9d64268",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1198,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 1198,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "0126c8bd69834d506a6d5ecd5db4bc3838d6fd3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "428d3fff_cd813a54",
        "filename": "common/keyboard_8042.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-12T01:11:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you do \u0027const int array_size \u003d ARRAY_SIZE(kblog.ringbuf)\u0027, I believe the compiler should just replace it with a constant. So, you wouldn\u0027t use memory.",
      "parentUuid": "20a38ccf_04dba05a",
